<section class="content-section">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:860px">

    <p>Searching for the <strong>best hospital in Ahmedabad</strong> usually starts with a specific need — a parent who needs a knee replaced, a family looking for a hospital with a 24-hour emergency department, or a patient whose insurer wants a NABH-accredited facility for a cashless claim. There isn't a single hospital that is "best" for every situation; the right choice depends on the specialty required, how urgent the case is, and what the patient's insurance or budget allows.</p>

    <p>DHS Multispecialty Hospital is a NABH-accredited, 50-bed hospital in the Vastrapur–Gurukul area of Ahmedabad, offering 15+ medical specialties, round-the-clock emergency and ICU care, and a dedicated orthopaedic program built around VELYS robotic-assisted knee replacement. This page explains what to look for in a hospital, what DHS actually offers, and how to reach us — so you can judge for yourself whether we're the right fit for your care.</p>

    <h2>What should you consider when choosing a hospital in Ahmedabad?</h2>
    <p>A few practical questions narrow the choice quickly:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Does it treat your specific condition?</strong> A cardiac emergency, a fracture, and a planned joint replacement need different departments, equipment and specialists.</li>
      <li><strong>Is it accredited?</strong> NABH (National Accreditation Board for Hospitals &amp; Healthcare Providers) certification means a hospital has been independently assessed against national patient-safety and quality standards — it's a useful, verifiable filter.</li>
      <li><strong>Can it handle emergencies?</strong> Check whether emergency care, an ICU and an operation theatre are available 24×7, not just during OPD hours.</li>
      <li><strong>How far is it, and can family reach it easily?</strong> For planned surgery and for follow-up visits, a hospital that's easy to reach matters, especially for senior patients.</li>
      <li><strong>Does it accept your insurance?</strong> Confirm cashless empanelment with your insurer or TPA before admission wherever possible.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>With those filters in mind, here is what DHS Multispecialty Hospital offers.</p>

    <h2>Why patients consider DHS Multispecialty Hospital</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>NABH-accredited, 50-bed multispecialty hospital</strong> in Ahmedabad, built around 15+ clinical departments under one roof.</li>
      <li><strong>24×7 emergency care, ICU and operation theatres</strong> — not limited to OPD hours.</li>
      <li><strong>A dedicated orthopaedic and robotic joint-replacement program</strong> led by Medical Director <a href="/doctors/doctor-hardik/">Dr. Hardik M Shah</a>, using VELYS robotic-assisted technology from Johnson &amp; Johnson.</li>
      <li><strong>Cashless treatment</strong> with major general insurers and TPA partners, with PMJAY support.</li>
      <li><strong>A single, accessible campus</strong> in Vastrapur / Gurukul, Ahmedabad, so emergency, diagnostics, surgery and follow-up all happen in one place.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Each of these is explained in more detail below.</p>

    <h2>NABH accreditation and hospital standards</h2>
    <p>NABH accreditation is granted by India's national board for healthcare quality and is based on an audit of a hospital's patient-safety protocols, infection control practices, clinical documentation, staff qualification checks and facility standards. It does not guarantee any specific medical outcome, but it is a meaningful, independently verified baseline — which is why many insurers prefer or require NABH status for cashless empanelment.</p>
    <p>DHS Multispecialty Hospital is NABH-accredited. In practice, this means standardised protocols for infection control, medication safety, patient identification and documentation are followed across our wards, ICU and operation theatres, and are reviewed periodically as part of maintaining accreditation.</p>

    <h2>A 50-bed multispecialty hospital, built for continuity of care</h2>
    <p>DHS is a 50-bed hospital, which keeps emergency response, diagnostics, surgery, ICU and inpatient recovery within one campus rather than spread across multiple facilities. That matters most when a case starts in the emergency room and needs to move quickly to imaging, then to an operation theatre, then to the ICU — the same clinical team and records follow the patient through each step.</p>
    <p>The campus includes dedicated operation theatres, an 8-bed ICU, an in-house radiology and laboratory setup, an in-house pharmacy, and a 24×7 ambulance service for emergency transport.</p>

    <h2>Medical specialties and departments</h2>
    <p>DHS runs 15+ clinical departments, broadly grouped as:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Orthopaedics and musculoskeletal care</strong> — orthopaedics, robotic joint replacement, trauma, arthroscopy, spine surgery, sports medicine</li>
      <li><strong>Internal medicine and surgical specialties</strong> — general surgery, internal medicine, gastro surgery, urology, vascular surgery, cosmetology &amp; plastic surgery</li>
      <li><strong>Organ and system-specific care</strong> — cardiology, neurosurgery, cancer surgery, pulmonology, nephrology &amp; dialysis</li>
      <li><strong>Critical care and diagnostics</strong> — ICU &amp; critical care, radiology, pathology laboratory</li>
    </ul>
    <p>See the full list, with what each department treats, on our <a href="/departments/">departments page</a>.</p>

    <h2>Orthopaedics and robotic knee replacement</h2>
    <p>Orthopaedics is DHS's most established specialty. The program is led by Medical Director <a href="/doctors/doctor-hardik/">Dr. Hardik M Shah</a>, alongside the hospital's joint-replacement team, and has been involved in over 2,000 knee replacement procedures. The department covers fracture and trauma care, arthroscopy, spine surgery, sports injuries, and both conventional and robotic-assisted joint replacement.</p>
    <p>Read more on our <a href="/orthopedic-surgeon-ahmedabad/">orthopaedic surgeon page</a> or the <a href="/knee-replacement-ahmedabad/">knee replacement program page</a>, including recovery timelines and <a href="/cost-insurance-guide-knee-replacement-ahmedabad/">cost and insurance guidance</a>.</p>

    <h2>VELYS robotic-assisted knee replacement by Johnson &amp; Johnson</h2>
    <p>DHS offers VELYS, an imageless robotic-assistance system from Johnson &amp; Johnson's DePuy Synthes, for knee replacement surgery. "Imageless" means the system does not require a pre-operative CT scan — instead, it builds a 3D map of the patient's knee anatomy in real time, during the surgery itself, using digital probes and sensors referenced against the patient's own joint.</p>
    <p>That real-time, intra-operative mapping is used to guide implant positioning and alignment with the surgeon in control throughout — the robotic arm assists precision, it does not operate independently. Patients avoid the extra radiation, cost and scheduling step of a separate pre-op CT scan, and the surgical team works from live anatomical data rather than an image taken days or weeks earlier. Individual recovery still depends on the patient's age, bone quality and overall health, so outcomes are discussed case by case with the surgical team.</p>
    <p>Full details are on our <a href="/velys-robotic-knee-replacement-ahmedabad/">VELYS robotic knee replacement page</a>.</p>

    <h2>24×7 emergency and critical care</h2>
    <p>DHS runs a 24×7 emergency department with an on-call team and ambulance service, for both general medical emergencies and orthopaedic trauma such as fractures and road-traffic injuries. Emergency cases are triaged on arrival and, where needed, moved directly to the ICU or an operation theatre without waiting for the next OPD slot.</p>
    <p>More on our emergency and trauma protocols is on the <a href="/emergency-orthopedic-care-ahmedabad/">24×7 emergency orthopedic care page</a>. For a medical emergency, call <a href="tel:{{ site.phones.emergency | replace(' ', '') }}">{{ site.phones.emergency }}</a> (24x7).</p>

    <h2>ICU and operation theatre facilities</h2>
    <p>The hospital's ICU has 8 critical-care beds with ventilator support, central monitoring and HEPA filtration to reduce cross-infection risk, staffed around the clock. Dedicated operation theatres support both emergency surgery and planned procedures, including robotic-assisted joint replacement.</p>
    <p>Read more about critical-care protocols on our <a href="/departments/icu-critical-care/">ICU &amp; critical care department page</a>.</p>

    <h2>Diagnostic and support services</h2>
    <p>On-campus support services include a radiology department (X-ray, ultrasound and CT imaging), an in-house diagnostic laboratory, an in-house pharmacy for round-the-clock medicine access, and a 24×7 ambulance service with trained paramedical staff for emergency transport. Keeping these services on-site reduces the time between a doctor's order and a result or a medicine reaching the patient.</p>

    <h2>Insurance and cashless facilities</h2>
    <p>DHS offers cashless treatment through tie-ups with major general insurers — including HDFC Ergo, Bajaj Allianz, TATA AIG, SBI General, National Insurance, Oriental Insurance, The New India Assurance and United India — along with a wide network of TPA (Third Party Administrator) partners, and PMJAY (Ayushman Bharat) support for eligible patients. Our billing team helps verify eligibility and paperwork before admission wherever possible.</p>
    <p>See the current list of empaneled insurers and TPAs, and how the cashless process works, on our <a href="/cashless/">cashless &amp; insurance page</a>.</p>

    <h2>Patient experience and reviews</h2>
    <p>Beyond infrastructure and accreditation, how a hospital treats patients and families day-to-day — communication before surgery, clarity on costs, and support during recovery — is part of what people weigh when they call a hospital "the best" for their situation. Patients and families share their experience with DHS on <a href="{{ site.google_reviews_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google</a> and on our <a href="/testimonials/">patient testimonials page</a>; we encourage you to read a range of them rather than relying on any single review.</p>

    <h2>Hospital location and accessibility</h2>
    <p>DHS Multispecialty Hospital is located at {{ site.address.full }}. The campus sits in the Vastrapur–Gurukul area, close to Vastrapur Lake, with on-site parking and access from the Drive-in Road corridor. For directions, parking details and OPD timings, open <a href="{{ site.google_reviews_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DHS Multispecialty Hospital on Google Maps</a>, see our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>, or call <a href="tel:{{ site.phones.landline1 | replace('(', '') | replace(')', '') | replace(' ', '') }}">{{ site.phones.landline1 }}</a> (emergency 24x7: <a href="tel:{{ site.phones.emergency | replace(' ', '') }}">{{ site.phones.emergency }}</a>) / email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.</p>

